<title>FINLAND: Kesko says EU may object to Tuko merger.</title>
<headline>Kesko says EU may object to Tuko merger.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish wholesaler Kesko Oy said in a statement on Wednesday the European Commission may find its merger with Tuko is against merger legislation and that it would defend itself and negotiate changes.</p>
<p>&quot;The concentration may ... be regarded as inappropriate in the EU's merger legislation,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>The EU commission had made a preliminary finding that the new group could lead to or strengthen a dominating market position which may significantly hinder competition in Finland, Kesko said.</p>
<p>&quot;Kesko has a totally different view and Kesko will give a statement of defence and negotiate with the commission on changes to the merger arrangement so that it could approve it,&quot; Kesko said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
